  "question": {
    "text": "In the precipitation of the iron group (III) in qualitative analysis, ammonium chloride is added before adding ammonium hydroxide to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EATVH",
      "text": "increase concentration of \\(\\mathrm{Cl}^{-}\\)ions",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "A1qFI",
      "text": "increase concentration of \\(\\mathrm{NH}_4{ }^{+}\\)ions",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rL9U9",
      "text": "prevent interference by phosphate ions",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gooqr",
      "text": "decrease concentration of \\({ }^{-} \\mathrm{OH}\\) ions",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{Cl} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}+\\mathrm{Cl}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Due to common ion effect of $\\mathrm{NH}_4^{+}$,\n$\\left[\\mathrm{OH}^{-}\\right]$decreases in such extent that only group-III cation can be precipitated, due to their very low $\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}$ in the range of $10^{-38}$.",
    "image": null
  },
